This repository uses more than one license. Every source file states its
license in an SPDX-License-Identifier line at the top of the file, and the
full license texts are in the LICENSES/ directory:

  GPL-2.0   LICENSES/GPL-2.0   GNU General Public License, version 2 only
  MIT       LICENSES/MIT       MIT License

Current assignment:

  driver/triple.c                    GPL-2.0  (Linux kernel module)
  driver/triple_proto.c              MIT      (protocol codec)
  driver/include/triple_proto.h      MIT      (protocol codec)
  gui/savvycan/                      MIT      (SavvyCAN connection)
  tools/                             MIT      (Python codec and tools)
  tests/                             MIT
  driver/Makefile, driver/dkms.conf  GPL-2.0  (module build files)
  ci/, scripts/, etc/, .github/      MIT      (build, CI and system integration)

The kernel module built from driver/ is licensed as a whole under
GPL-2.0; the MIT licensed codec it includes is compatible with that.

Documentation (doc/, README files) is provided under the MIT license as
well, unless a file says otherwise.

Earlier versions of this repository (before the v2.0 driver) were
distributed with a GNU General Public License version 3 text; their
source files stated "GPL version 2 or later". That history is unchanged.
